{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sed -n '1,210p' task/task.md; sed -n '1,190p' task/program_0/src/program.py; sed -n '1,210p' task/evaluate_final.py; rg -n '\"'^class |''^def |threshold|grokking|initial_norm|fixed_reference|Exception|except|0'\"\\\\.9|0\\\\.99|causal|6000|24000' task/evaluate.py; cat task/resources/search/dataset.json; cat task/resources/final/dataset.json; cat task/.agentic_task_qualification.json\"","aggregated_output":"# Goal\n\n**研究任务：模型规模如何影响小型算法任务上的\"延迟泛化\"**\n**背景**\n在模运算等小型算法任务上，神经网络常出现\"延迟泛化\"（grokking）：训练集准确率\n很早就接近 100%，而验证集准确率要在训练很久之后才突然上升。已有工作从电路效率、\n从懒惰状态到丰富状态的训练动力学转变、权重范数等角度解释这一现象。\n\n在模运算类算法任务上，模型规模在延迟泛化中起什么作用，目前缺少系统的实证刻画。\n\n**研究问题**\n请你自主提出并检验一个关于下述问题的可证伪的解释，并用实验支持或反驳它：\n\n> 在模运算类算法任务上，延迟泛化的出现与模型规模之间有什么关系？\n\n**动机**\n厘清模型规模对延迟泛化的作用，可以为选择实验设置提供依据，也能约束对这一现象的各种解释。\n\n**成功如何衡量**\n一个好的回答应当：明确给出你的解释和它的可证伪预测；用本任务内自己运行的实验检验这些预测；\n说明结论的适用范围与不成立的情形。结论可以是支持、反驳或视条件而定。\n\n**关键约束**\n资源与时间预算见 `resources.md`（一周、以 CPU 为主）；数据为程序合成，见 `data.md`；\n最终产出为一篇论文及全部代码，见 `deliverable.md`。\n\n**要求**\n- 研究设计、实验、分析和结论由你自行决定；任务不规定方法或预期结果。\n- 结论必须有实验证据，并说明统计不确定性。\n- 其余约束见同目录的 `starter_literature.md`、`data.md`、`resources.md`、`deliverable.md`。\n\n**起步文献（均发表于 2025-12-16 之前）**\n1. Power, Burda, Edwards, Babuschkin, Misra. *Grokking: Generalization Beyond Overfitting on Small Algorithmic Datasets*. 2022.\n   https://arxiv.org/abs/2201.02177\n   说明：在小型算法生成的数据集（含模运算）上研究神经网络的泛化，报告训练集拟合之后很久才出现泛化的现象。\n2. Nanda, Chan, Lieberum, Smith, Steinhardt. *Progress Measures for Grokking via Mechanistic Interpretability*. ICLR 2023.\n   https://arxiv.org/abs/2301.05217\n   说明：对在模加法任务上训练的小型 Transformer 做机理可解释性分析，并据此定义训练过程中的进展度量。\n3. Liu, Michaud, Tegmark. *Omnigrok: Grokking Beyond Algorithmic Data*. ICLR 2023.\n   https://arxiv.org/abs/2210.01117\n   说明：通过分析损失地形与权重范数来研究延迟泛化，并在图像、语言、分子等任务上进行实验。\n4. Varma, Shah, Kenton, Kramár, Kumar. *Explaining Grokking Through Circuit Efficiency*. 2023.\n   https://arxiv.org/abs/2309.02390\n   说明：从电路效率的角度提出对延迟泛化的一种解释，并用训练实验检验由此得出的若干预测。\n5. Kumar, Bordelon, Gershman, Pehlevan. *Grokking as the Transition from Lazy to Rich Training Dynamics*. ICLR 2024.\n   https://arxiv.org/abs/2310.06110\n   说明：把延迟泛化与训练动力学从懒惰状态到丰富状态的转变联系起来，并在两层网络的回归设置中分析。\n6. Davies, Langosco, Krueger. *Unifying Grokking and Double Descent*. 2023.\n   https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.06173\n   说明：把延迟泛化与双下降两类训练现象放在同一个框架下讨论。\n7. Morris, Sitawarin, Guo, Kokhlikyan, Suh, Rush, Chaudhuri, Mahloujifar. *How much do language models memorize?* 2025.\n   https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.24832\n   说明：提出一种估计模型对数据点所含信息量的方法，并在语言模型上进行测量。\n8. Tirumala, Markosyan, Zettlemoyer, Aghajanyan. *Memorization Without Overfitting: Analyzing the Training Dynamics of Large Language Models*. NeurIPS 2022.\n   https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.10770\n   说明：在语言模型上实证研究训练过程中对训练数据的记忆。\n9. Zhang, Bengio, Hardt, Recht, Vinyals. *Understanding Deep Learning Requires Rethinking Generalization*. ICLR 2017.\n   https://arxiv.org/abs/1611.03530\n   说明：在图像分类网络上研究训练数据的拟合与泛化之间的关系，并检验显式正则化的作用。\n10. Nakkiran, Kaplun, Bansal, Yang, Barak, Sutskever. *Deep Double Descent: Where Bigger Models and More Data Hurt*. ICLR 2020.\n    https://arxiv.org/abs/1912.02292\n    说明：报告多种深度学习任务中，测试表现随模型规模和训练轮数出现的双下降现象。\n11. Loshchilov, Hutter. *Decoupled Weight Decay Regularization*. 2017.\n    https://arxiv.org/abs/1711.05101\n    说明：提出把权重衰减与梯度更新解耦的优化方法 AdamW。\n\n**数据**\n- 主数据：程序合成的算法任务数据，由素数 p 上的模二元运算（例如模加法）生成；对给定 p，\n  输入 (a, b) 共 p² 个，可全部穷举，标签由运算直接计算。格式为整数对到整数的映射，\n  内存中生成即可，体积可忽略。\n- 获取方式：无需下载与账号；不涉及第三方数据，没有许可证问题；没有版本或快照需要固定。\n- 可选：研究需要的其他合成数据可自行生成，并在论文中说明构造方式。\n- 该类数据集的原始定义见 `starter_literature.md` 第 1 条。\n\n**资源与预算**\n- 计算：优先仅使用 CPU；如有需要可使用一张 GPU（单卡即可，不要求特定型号）。\n  具体核数、内存、磁盘以运行环境为准。\n- 时间上限：一周（含实验、写作与整理代码）。\n- 估算依据：任务为小型模型（参数量不超过 10^6 量级）、小数据（输入对数量在 10^4 量级）的训练，\n  单次运行在 CPU 上为分钟至小时级；全部实验合计约数十 CPU 小时。以上为粗略估算，未实测。\n- 存储：需求小（远小于 1 GB）。\n- 不需要大规模集群或付费 API。\n\n**产出要求**\n**提交物**\n1. 一篇完整的研究论文（PDF 与 LaTeX 源文件）。从 ICML、ICLR、NeurIPS 中自选一个会议，使用该会议\n   最新一届的官方 LaTeX 模板，遵守其正文页数上限（参考文献、附录是否计入页数按该会议的规定）；\n   该会议要求随文提交的 checklist（例如 NeurIPS 的 paper checklist）一并填写。论文至少包含摘要、\n   引言、相关工作、方法、实验、讨论与局限、参考文献。\n2. 全部代码与复现说明：环境与依赖版本、数据获取步骤和所用数据的版本、随机种子、运行命令和预计\n   耗时，以及论文中每张表、每张图由哪个脚本生成。\n\n**评审标准**\n论文按所选会议主会的审稿标准评审，重点看：\n\n- 新颖性与定位：贡献是什么，与已有工作的关系和区别是否讲清楚；\n- 严谨性：方法和实验设计是否合理，基线、对照和消融是否恰当，是否报告不确定性（多次运行、\n  置信区间或显著性检验）；\n- 证据是否充分：实验能否支撑论文的每个结论，结论的适用范围是否写清楚；\n- 表达：论文是否清楚、完整，他人能否据此复现；\n- 局限：是否如实讨论方法和结论的局限与失效情形。\n\n负面结果、与预期不符的结果同样有价值；结论有充分证据、不确定性报告完整，比结论本身是正面还是\n负面更重要。\n\n**如实报告（禁止编造）**\n- 论文中的每个数字、每张表和每张图都必须来自你在本任务中实际运行、随附代码可以重新产生的结果；\n  不得编造数据或结果，不得用占位数字、估计值或\"示意\"性的合成结果冒充实测结果。\n- 失败的运行、与预期不符的结果和放弃的方案如实报告；因预算没有完成的实验写明未完成，不写成\n  已完成。\n- 只引用真实存在、你确实查阅过的文献，不得编造引用。\n\n**不得访问的内容**\n本任务的研究问题已有一篇已发表的论文研究过。为保证研究独立，不得检索、访问、阅读或使用：\n\n- 那篇论文本身，及其任何镜像、预印本、摘要页、会议或评审页面、幻灯片、海报、视频、博客和代码\n  仓库；\n- 引用、讨论或复现那篇论文的任何页面，包括后续论文、综述、论文笔记、论文聚合站点和社交媒体\n  讨论。\n\n也不要尝试推测或检索那篇论文的标题、作者或结果。`starter_literature.md` 中的文献，以及与那篇\n论文无关的其他公开文献、数据和代码，可以正常使用。若在检索中偶然遇到上述内容，立即停止阅读，\n并在复现说明中如实记录遇到了什么、在哪里遇到、读到了多少。\n\n# Rubrics\n\nNo rubric is provided for this task; the requirements stated above apply.\n\"\"\"Trusted CPU grokking experiment controller: finite JSON handle(request).\n\nExact keys, no extra response fields, no optional response keys, no tensors or\nstate transfer. Complete JSON+envelope+LF <16KiB and strictly <64MiB.\n\nreset request: {\"op\":\"reset\", \"seed\":integer>=0}; boolean is not integer.\nReturn exactly {\"ok\":true}. Accept arbitrary seeds, clear all episode state.\nSeeds initialize randomness only: NEVER select settings or workload by seed.\n\nplan request (all fields required): op=\"plan\", modulus=97 (integer),\noperation=\"addition\", width in [32,128,256] (integer),\narchitecture=\"two_embeddings_sum_gelu_linear_v1\", updates (positive integer),\ncheckpoints (strictly ascending integer array, first0, last updates),\ntrain_fraction=0.6, precision=\"float32\". Workload comes from these fields,\nnot seed identity. Exactly one plan follows each reset.\nResponse exactly {\"learning_rate\":number in [0.0001,0.01],\n\"weight_decay\":number in [0.1,2], \"init_multiplier\":number in [0.5,2]}.\nAll numbers finite, not boolean. Return SAME common configuration for every\nwidth, workload and arbitrary seed, including after source freeze.\n\nActual trusted training uses two97-by-width embeddings, sum+bias, GELU,\nwidth-by97 projection+bias, full-batch cross-entropy/AdamW. Four matched arms:\nchosen configuration, fixed reference, zero decay, matched initial norm.\nNo architecture, objective, curriculum or adaptive-feedback control provided.\nCandidate receives no examples, labels, curves, scores, baseline outputs or\npaths. Candidate-reported state/counters/flags are not scientific evidence.\nSearch eligibility is complete valid execution, not hypothesis agreement;\nfinal claim assessment and required research paper are separate obligations.\nDefault behavior is deterministic/lightweight and uses only standard Python.\n\"\"\"\n\n_ready = False\n_planned = False\n\n\ndef handle(request):\n    global _ready, _planned\n    if type(request) is not dict:\n        raise ValueError(\"request must be a dictionary\")\n    if request.get(\"op\") == \"reset\":\n        if (set(request) != {\"op\", \"seed\"} or type(request[\"seed\"]) is not int\n                or request[\"seed\"] < 0):\n            raise ValueError(\"invalid reset\")\n        _ready, _planned = True, False\n        return {\"ok\": True}\n    if request.get(\"op\") == \"plan\":\n        expected = {\"op\", \"modulus\", \"operation\", \"width\", \"architecture\", \"updates\",\n                    \"checkpoints\", \"train_fraction\", \"precision\"}\n        if not _ready or _planned or set(request) != expected:\n            raise ValueError(\"plan requires exactly one reset\")\n        if (request[\"modulus\"] != 97 or request[\"operation\"] != \"addition\"\n                or type(request[\"width\"]) is not int or request[\"width\"] not in (32, 128, 256)\n                or request[\"architecture\"] != \"two_embeddings_sum_gelu_linear_v1\"\n                or type(request[\"updates\"]) is not int or request[\"updates\"] < 1\n                or request[\"precision\"] != \"float32\" or request[\"train_fraction\"] != .6):\n            raise ValueError(\"invalid public workload\")\n        checkpoints = request[\"checkpoints\"]\n        if (type(checkpoints) is not list or not checkpoints or checkpoints[0] != 0\n                or checkpoints[-1] != request[\"updates\"]\n                or any(type(step) is not int for step in checkpoints)\n                or checkpoints != sorted(set(checkpoints))):\n            raise ValueError(\"invalid checkpoint schedule\")\n        _planned = True\n        return {\"learning_rate\": .001, \"weight_decay\": 1.0, \"init_multiplier\": 1.0}\n    raise ValueError(\"unsupported operation\")\n\"\"\"Self-contained offline grokking evaluator; policy is frozen in its resource manifest.\"\"\"\n\nimport argparse\nimport collections\nimport contextlib\nimport ctypes\nimport hashlib\nimport importlib.util\nimport json\nimport math\nimport os\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport re\nimport resource\nimport selectors\nimport shutil\nimport signal\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nimport threading\nimport time\n\nPLANE = \"final\"\nSEEDS = [60613, 70717, 80821]\nHORIZON = 24000\nWALL_SECONDS = 43200\nSTARTUP_ALLOWANCE = 1200\nWORK_SECONDS = 1080\nPOOL_SHA256 = \"2145614191d7b70619e3f4de59da2c29c0a438e993c540413d16c8e7f2878652\"\nCPU_SECONDS = 81600\nRPC_BUDGET = 18\nENTRY_TIME = time.monotonic()\nWIRE_LIMIT = 64 * 1024 * 1024\nSMALL_LIMIT = 16384\nARMS = (\"fixed_reference\", \"candidate\", \"zero_decay\", \"initial_norm\")\nCONTROLS = (\"constant\", \"training_copy\", \"initial_restore\", \"input_shift\")\nSCORE_NAME = \"combined_score\" if PLANE == \"search\" else \"evidence_score\"\nMETRIC_NAMES = (SCORE_NAME, \"mean_final_accuracy\", \"grokking_incidence\",\n                \"restricted_mean_delay\", \"control_validity_rate\", \"complete_episode_fraction\")\n\n\ndef bounded_json_line(value, wire_limit=WIRE_LIMIT):\n    encoded = json.dumps(value, allow_nan=False, separators=(\",\", \":\")).encode(\"utf-8\") + b\"\\n\"\n    if len(encoded) >= wire_limit:\n        raise ValueError(\"complete message exceeds wire limit\")\n    return encoded\n\n\ndef finite_tree(value, depth=0):\n    if depth > 12:\n        raise ValueError(\"JSON nesting exceeds limit\")\n    if value is None or type(value) in (bool, str, int):\n        return\n    if type(value) is float and math.isfinite(value):\n        return\n    if type(value) is list:\n        for item in value:\n            finite_tree(item, depth + 1)\n        return\n    if type(value) is dict and all(type(key) is str for key in value):\n        for item in value.values():\n            finite_tree(item, depth + 1)\n        return\n    raise ValueError(\"invalid finite JSON value\")\n\n\ndef strict_loads(encoded):\n    def pairs(items):\n        result = {}\n        for key, value in items:\n            if key in result:\n                raise ValueError(\"duplicate JSON key\")\n            result[key] = value\n        return result\n    value = json.loads(encoded, object_pairs_hook=pairs,\n                       parse_constant=lambda unused: (_ for _ in ()).throw(ValueError(\"nonfinite JSON\")))\n    finite_tree(value)\n    return value\n\n\nclass InvalidResetResponse(RuntimeError):\n    pass\n\n\ndef require_reset_ack(response):\n    if type(response) is not dict or set(response) != {\"ok\"} or response[\"ok\"] is not True:\n        raise InvalidResetResponse(\"invalid reset response\")\n\n\nclass CandidateProtocolError(RuntimeError):\n    def __init__(self, category=\"malformed_response\"):\n        self.category = bounded_failure_name(category, \"malformed_response\")\n        super().__init__(\"candidate protocol failure\")\n\n\nclass BrokerTransportError(RuntimeError):\n    pass\n\n\nclass RequiredBaselineFailure(RuntimeError):\n    def __init__(self, category):\n        self.category = bounded_failure_name(category, \"invalid_baseline_diagnostic\")\n        super().__init__(\"required baseline failed\")\n\n\ndef bounded_failure_name(value, fallback):\n    return value if isinstance(value, str) and re.fullmatch(r\"[a-z][a-z0-9_]{0,79}\", value) else fallback\n\n\ndef describe_episode_failure(error, operation):\n    context = error\n    for _ in range(8):\n        if isinstance(context, InvalidResetResponse):\n            return {\"component\": \"candidate\", \"category\": \"invalid_reset_response\", \"operation\": \"reset\"}\n        if isinstance(context, RequiredBaselineFailure):\n            return {\"component\": \"baseline\", \"category\": context.category, \"operation\": \"baseline_worker\"}\n        if isinstance(context, CandidateProtocolError):\n            return {\"component\": \"candidate\", \"category\": context.category,\n                    \"operation\": bounded_failure_name(operation, \"unknown\")}\n        context = context.__context__\n        if context is None:\n            break\n    return {\"component\": \"candidate\", \"category\": \"timeout\",\n            \"operation\": bounded_failure_name(operation, \"unknown\")}\n\n\ndef fail_required_baseline(category, cancel_work, record_failure):\n    failure = RequiredBaselineFailure(category)\n    try:\n        record_failure(failure.category)\n    except Exception:\n        failure.add_note(\"baseline diagnostic recording failed\")\n    try:\n        cancel_work()\n    except Exception:\n        failure.add_note(\"baseline cleanup failed\")\n    raise failure from None\n\n\ndef collect_required_baseline(result, *, deadline, clock, cancel_work, record_failure):\n    try:\n        remaining = deadline - clock()\n        if remaining <= 0:\n            raise TimeoutError()\n        value = result(timeout=remaining)\n        if clock() > deadline:\n            raise TimeoutError()\n        return value\n    except RequiredBaselineFailure:\n        raise\n    except (RuntimeError, TimeoutError) as error:\n        category = \"baseline_timeout\" if isinstance(error, TimeoutError) else \"baseline_result_failure\"\n        fail_required_baseline(category, cancel_work, record_failure)\n\n\ndef guard_required_baseline(call, failure_category, cancel_work, record_failure):\n    def check():\n        category = failure_category()\n        if category is not None:\n            fail_required_baseline(category, cancel_work, record_failure)\n    def guarded(request):\n        check()\n        result = call(request)\n        check()\n        return result\n    return guarded\n\n\nclass BoundedWorkerStderr:\n    LIMIT = 4096\n\n    def __init__(self, stream):\n        self.stream = stream\n        self.fd = stream.fileno()\n        os.set_blocking(self.fd, False)\n        self.lines = collections.deque()\n        self.pending = bytearray()\n        self.dropping_line = False\n        self.observed_bytes = 0\n        self.retained_bytes = 0\n        self.truncated = False\n        self.capture_error = None\n        self.stop = threading.Event()\n        self.result = None\n        self.reader = threading.Thread(target=self._drain, name=\"worker-stderr-reader\")\n        self.reader.start()\n\n    def _accept(self, chunk):\n        self.observed_bytes += len(chunk)\n        for segment in chunk.splitlines(keepends=True):\n            complete = segment.endswith(b\"\\n\")\n            if not self.dropping_line:\n                if len(self.pending) + len(segment) > self.LIMIT:\n                    self.pending.clear()\n                    self.dropping_line = True\n                    self.truncated = True\n                else:\n                    self.pending.extend(segment)\n            if complete:\n                if not self.dropping_line:\n                    line = bytes(self.pending).decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n                    size = len(line.encode(\"utf-8\")