\n        484,\n        2109,\n        289,\n        4621,\n        476,\n        1233,\n        2878,\n        1524,\n        1885,\n        60,\n        4629,\n        2526,\n        4548,\n        1309,\n        1297,\n        2860,\n        2910,\n        4210,\n        1131,\n        226,\n        4430,\n        1610,\n        883,\n        930,\n        3408,\n        2834,\n        72,\n        3694,\n        4477,\n        3652,\n        3210,\n        1928,\n        2209,\n        3863,\n        4557,\n        3110,\n        3492,\n        1644,\n        3759,\n        248,\n        4344,\n        4678,\n        1147,\n        304,\n        617,\n        865,\n        660,\n        1121,\n        2297,\n        4432,\n        3239,\n        1618,\n        3047,\n        2282,\n        1190,\n        24,\n        3064,\n        244,\n        481,\n        2492,\n        3941,\n        1924,\n        1614,\n        4142,\n        881,\n        3030,\n        380,\n        4419,\n        4143,\n        872,\n        428,\n        4015,\n        4700,\n        3794,\n        505,\n        1612,\n        1226,\n        621,\n        4144,\n        2858,\n        432,\n        3814,\n        860,\n        1362,\n        2741,\n        4682,\n        3380,\n        2848,\n        671,\n        1632,\n        3269,\n        1915,\n        2169,\n        623,\n        3177,\n        4078,\n        2486,\n        3122,\n        4566,\n        1949,\n        4362,\n        3960,\n        4041,\n        1207,\n        3656,\n        2721,\n        4134,\n        1235,\n        1722,\n        4506,\n        4532,\n        4698,\n        3608,\n        3136,\n        4207,\n        4252,\n        3418,\n        3637,\n        878,\n        4280,\n        1064,\n        2700,\n        1827,\n        1673,\n        3947,\n        175,\n        2500,\n        2621,\n        4181,\n        436,\n        3993,\n        3312,\n        311,\n        2705,\n        1428,\n        302,\n        3154,\n        2679,\n        1686,\n        3391,\n        766,\n        1473,\n        897,\n        2312,\n        330,\n        247,\n        2401,\n        2617,\n        3806,\n        2135,\n        1095,\n        2995,\n        1908,\n        2961,\n        235,\n        4388,\n        4525,\n        2948,\n        892,\n        2001,\n        759,\n        1723,\n        3187\n      ],\n      \"sha256\": \"06f2f20a81c868dda306469edebc72686cee5f259c7e1edf94ede674e49e0022\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"policy\": {\n    \"platform\": \"Linux x86_64 CPython3.12 CPU-only; evaluator2 threads/8GiB, candidate1 thread/1GiB. Native isolation requires LandlockABI3 and seccomp; fail closed. No runtime network/user-site.\",\n    \"normalization\": \"Canonical input compact UTF-8 JSON fixed key order operation,modulus,a,b (integer). Identity excludes IDs, paths, seeds, plane, targets. Separate raw example hash of [a,b,target] plus LF. No text; future text must NFKC and collapse Unicode whitespace before splitting/tokenization.\",\n    \"generator\": \"Enumerate p97 addition. Sort SHA256(b\\\"grokking-pool-v1\\\\0\\\"+canonical_input); first4704 search, remaining4705 final. Source row=a*97+b. Split sort SHA256(b\\\"grokking-split-v1\\\\0\\\"+decimal_seed+b\\\"\\\\0\\\"+canonical_input); floor(.6*N) train.\",\n    \"architecture\": \"Learned97-by-width embeddings for both inputs, sum+hidden bias, exactGELU, width-by97 projection+bias. 292*width+97 parameters. Float32 CPU full-batch cross-entropy, torch.optim.AdamW(foreach=False), all parameters including biases decayed.\",\n    \"initialization\": \"torch CPU generator(seed) draws first97x256, second97x256, output256x97 standard normals. Slice width columns/rows. Embeddings multiply init_multiplier; projection multiply init_multiplier/sqrt(width); biases zero. Coupled directions across widths/arms. Norm arm globally rescales all parameters to same-seed width128 norm at selected multiplier.\",\n    \"arm_order\": [\n      \"fixed_reference\",\n      \"candidate\",\n      \"zero_decay\",\n      \"initial_norm\"\n    ],\n    \"reference\": {\n      \"learning_rate\": 0.001,\n      \"weight_decay\": 1.0,\n      \"init_multiplier\": 1.0\n    },\n    \"controls\": [\n      \"constant\",\n      \"training_copy\",\n      \"initial_restore\",\n      \"input_shift\"\n    ],\n    \"control_expectations\": \"Every candidate checkpoint uses same evaluation rows/count. Constant=lowest training-majority class. Copy=training lookup with majority fallback, equals exact fallback evaluation accuracy. Restore archived evaluator-owned initial state to scratch and require exact original logits. Input shift(a,b)->((a+1)%97,b) bijective/nonidentity/answer-changing and actual trained forward. If parent accuracy>=.95, diagnostic drop supported iff shift_accuracy<=.1 and drop>=.8; otherwise inconclusive. Mechanical validity, not desired outcome, gates eligibility. Identity/label-preserving/omitted controls invalid.\",\n    \"events\": \"Step0 and every100 updates. Train>=.99, eval>=.95 sustained3 checkpoints; onset first of3. Grokking iff both observed and nonnegative delay>=1000 updates. Otherwise right censor. Restricted delay=1 if either onset missing, else max(0,generalization-fit)/horizon. Keep censor flags; cap is not observed time. Smoke checkpoints0..4 after4 updates cannot certify production.\",\n    \"aggregation\": \"Equal checkpoints per arm, equal4 arms trajectory coverage; equal checkpoints and4 controls validity coverage. Episode=.5*trajectory+.25*controls+.25*candidate final accuracy. Seed-equal within width, width-equal. Balanced design equals fixed episode mean; smoke identity. Failed episode retains full weight score/accuracy/incidence/controls/completeness0, delay1. No dropping or renormalizing failures.\",\n    \"statistics\": \"Seed-paired wide256-minus-narrow32 contrasts in normalized fit, generalization and restricted delay. Interactions subtract zero-decay and norm-arm width contrasts. Censored onset assigned horizon only for restricted comparisons with censor flags retained. Exact empirical paired seed-bootstrap enumeration with replacement and conservative floor/ceil percentile indices at .025/.975. Report all seed values and low resolution. No checkpoint/example pseudoreplication.\",\n    \"search_correct\": \"All episodes/real arms/updates/controls complete, common allowed plan, finite trusted measurements, data/split integrity, exact transcript and budgets. No comparative, hypothesis sign, significance, novelty or grokking gate.\",\n    \"final_correct\": \"All final episodes and baselines/controls complete with frozen source, allowed common plan, final integrity and exact budgets/transcript. Not hypothesis acceptance/publication. Cross-plane plan equivalence must additionally be audited from released evidence; no supported cross-plane configuration carrier exists for these self-contained evaluators.\",\n    \"rpc_operation_table\": {\n      \"per_episode\": {\n        \"reset\": 1,\n        \"plan\": 1,\n        \"training\": 0,\n        \"rollouts\": 0,\n        \"controls\": 0,\n        \"transfers\": 0,\n        \"replay\": 0\n      },\n      \"wire\": \"No binary/state transfer allowed or needed, base64 bytes0; conservative protocol/id metadata+JSON+LF <16384 and strictly<67108864 bytes.\"\n    },\n    \"scheduling\": \"Single monotonic deadline includes conservative startup; finish60s. Global reset5s+overhead16s reservations. Overhead sums four worker cleanups3s each+candidate cleanup3s+dispatch1s; TERM.5+KILL/reap.5+stderr<=.4 each. Equal per-method productive work allowance and later-arm reservations. Reference first exercises actual update/evaluation path. Preserve failures, continue resets/plans. No replay.\",\n    \"joint_budget\": {\n      \"search\": {\n        \"episode_count\": 6,\n        \"method_count\": 4,\n        \"wall_seconds\": 14400,\n        \"startup_seconds\": 600,\n        \"reset_seconds\": 21,\n        \"cleanup_seconds\": 3,\n        \"finish_seconds\": 60,\n        \"work_seconds\": 480\n      },\n      \"final\": {\n        \"episode_count\": 9,\n        \"method_count\": 4,\n        \"wall_seconds\": 43200,\n        \"startup_seconds\": 1200,\n        \"reset_seconds\": 21,\n        \"cleanup_seconds\": 3,\n        \"finish_seconds\": 60,\n        \"work_seconds\": 1080\n      }\n    },\n    \"limitations\": [\n      \"Only addition p97, fixed architecture, limited seeds and finite horizons; no universal scaling or internal mechanism proof.\",\n      \"Scaffold is not the required paper. Publication needs latest official conference template, honest PDF/LaTeX/checklist/code and tables from actual task-run evidence.\",\n      \"Production throughput projected from reduced same-path calibration only, not full-horizon qualification.\",\n      \"Bounded hyperparameter controller only; no adaptive feedback, objectives, curricula or architecture API.\",\n      \"No research browsing during drafting; forbidden prior work not sought. Shared immutable code is not held-out data.\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"audit\": {\n    \"cross_plane_content_disjoint\": true,\n    \"input_intersection_count\": 0,\n    \"example_intersection_count\": 0,\n    \"own_normalized_hash_set_sha256\": \"22c77f7eb0061422cc7eb4834b0eb50dc9ba04edb8e416d9b529c4f01681bbae\",\n    \"method\": \"Privileged draft enumerated full source, hashed normalized raw inputs and examples before split, compared both sets ignoring IDs, checked provenance and per-seed split disjointness. Resource exposes only own pool and audit result.\"\n  }\n}\n{\n  \"accelerator_model\": \"none\",\n  \"baseline_combined_score\": 0.7779622741764081,\n  \"baseline_correct\": true,\n  \"baseline_feasible\": true,\n  \"candidate_gpu_count\": 0,\n  \"evaluator_gpu_count\": 0,\n  \"evaluator_tree_sha256\": \"9f151e5137d8bbd13d9c9b2b82a2a3a452255ed0311d927b3e8d5b39d5d125fa\",\n  \"image_id\": \"sha256:c957359c87fc067a97a5b85deb1f3d0ce1578a8b7d531