{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"python .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py --global-memory-md ./global_memory/memory.md --global-memory-jsonl ./global_memory/memory.jsonl --event-json '{\\\"step\\\":\\\"paper\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"paper\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Framing audit favors a bounded width-and-horizon study over a mechanistic or optimization-success narrative; gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=Framing does not establish a new experimental recommendation.\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"Final evaluation status completed, outcome not_qualified, correct false independently of search; downstream_study absent. Retained final evidence contains five of nine planned width-seed records: three width-32 censored records, two width-128 delayed events, no width-256 records. Four comparison arms exist and matched-norm duplicates the selected arm at width128. Supplied ICLR style has single-column textwidth5.5in and textheight9in. No prior manuscript or staged edit context found.\\\",\\\"next_action\\\":\\\"Audit trusted metric definitions and source identifiers; build a thesis-first strategy preserving qualification failure, incomplete coverage, controls, and uncertainty without a causal scaling claim.\\\"}'\npython - <<'PY'\nimport json\np=json.load(open('paper_data.json'))\nprint('ground source IDs',list(p['grounding_sources']))\nfor path in ['task/resources/search/dataset.json','task/resources/final/dataset.json']:\n d=json.load(open(path)); print('\\\\n',path,'keys',list(d))\n for k,v in d.items():\n  if isinstance(v,list): print(k,'len',len(v))\n  elif isinstance(v,dict): print(k,'keys',list(v))\n  else: print(k,str(v)[:150])\n for sub in d.values():\n  if isinstance(sub,dict):\n   for k in ['architecture','model','events','statistics','aggregation','initialization','reference','training','seeds','widths','horizon','checkpoints','search_correct','final_correct']:\n    if k in sub: print(k,sub[k])\nr