the two horizons as separate evidence blocks under one question: data pools and seed sets also change. No same-seed, same-pool horizon intervention or causal claim that longer training reverses a width ranking is available.',\n        'The intended final width-256-minus-width-32 contrast and corresponding interactions are unidentified because width-256 records are absent; final paired_contrasts are null. Missing records are not zero accuracy observations, right-censored trajectories, or measured losses.',\n        'Show every seed value and paired differences where supported. Do not use checkpoints or examples as independent trials. Small-seed descriptive variation is the main uncertainty display; any additional uncertainty calculation must be derived reproducibly from retained data and labeled conditional on availability.'\n    ],\n    'figure_plan': [\n        'Figure 1: early overview of the modular-addition network, width/arm controls, and distinct observed-event/censored/missing evidence states; no speculative circuit or causal mechanism.',\n        'Figure 2: two aligned direct-comparison panels of raw endpoint held-out accuracy by width and four arms, one for short-horizon selection observations and one for final observations; preserve absent cells and separate cohorts.',\n        'Figure 3: two aligned onset-comparison panels for the studied configuration, showing training-fit and held-out-onset markers by width and seed, censoring at the relevant horizon, and missing final records without imputed times.'\n    ],\n    'figure_specs': [\n        {\n            'figure_id': 'study_overview',\n            'required': True,\n            'purpose': 'Make the fixed architecture, intervention scope, and evidence states legible before quantitative results.',\n            'figure_type': 'diagram',\n            'preferred_generator': 'generate-concept-figure',\n            'group_by': 'experimental_condition',\n            'metric': 'none; design and observation-state